stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> RelaxedIdle
    RelaxedIdle --> NormalWalk: movement / no cursor engagement
    NormalWalk --> Run: ordinary walk timer reaches 1.2 s
    RelaxedIdle --> Caution: movement toward or across acquired enemy cursor
    NormalWalk --> Caution: living enemy cursor acquired
    Run --> Caution: living enemy cursor acquired
    Caution --> RetreatHold: moving away or losing cursor
    RetreatHold --> Caution: reacquire target toward movement / reset timer
    RetreatHold --> Run: 500 ms continuous retreat elapsed
    NormalWalk --> RelaxedIdle: release movement
    Run --> RelaxedIdle: release movement
    Caution --> RelaxedIdle: release movement
    RetreatHold --> RelaxedIdle: release movement / reset elapsed retreat
    note right of RetreatHold
        Still uses caution animation and walking speed.
        Cursor loss does not skip the hold.
        Prior caution engagement is retained while stopped.
    end note
    note right of RelaxedIdle
        Proximity alone never readies weapon.
        Attack and reactions use companion diagrams.
    end note
